{"issues":[{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"14954","self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/14954","key":"MC-139548","renderedFields":{"summary":null,"issuetype":null,"watches":null,"customfield_10070":null,"customfield_10061":"","created":"17/Nov/18 12:10 PM","customfield_10050":"","customfield_10051":null,"description":"<h3><a name=\"Thebug\"></a>The bug</h3>\n<p>NOTE: This is <em>not</em> a duplicate of \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"MC-124197\">\n                <a href=\"https://mojira.atlassian.net/browse/MC-124197\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\" title=\"Arrow entitydata on server is not synced with client\">\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10303?size=medium\">\n            MC-124197\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Resolved</span>\n            </span>\n or any bugs listed within.  This is new as of the 1.14 snapshots.  It didn't occur in 1.13.2.</p>\n\n<p>It affects all projectile entities (e.g. arrows, fireballs, potions, enderpearls, snowballs, eggs, etc.) but not other entities such as tnt or mobs.  Every ~20 ticks it updates the position to where it's supposed to be, and if the entity changes state (such as an arrow's inGround tag becoming true) it updates immediately.  It also affects other entities properly even while not being rendered in the correct location.  For the Power<span class=\"error\">[0,1,2]</span> data, the projectile renders with a trajectory that curves towards the negative X, Y, and Z directions but actually travels and impacts as it should.</p>\n\n<p>A video's worth a thousand pictures, so here's a video showing the bug in action</p>\n\n<p><span class=\"nobr\"><a href=\"/rest/api/3/attachment/content/23419\" title=\"Minecraft 1.21.3 - Singleplayer 2024-10-25 22-05-25.mp4 attached to MC-139548\" data-attachment-type=\"file\" data-attachment-name=\"Minecraft 1.21.3 - Singleplayer 2024-10-25 22-05-25.mp4\" data-media-services-type=\"file\" data-media-services-id=\"c15ab6fe-980f-4244-b1c4-91e7e252eca1\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Video demonstration<sup><img class=\"rendericon\" src=\"/images/icons/link_attachment_7.gif\" height=\"7\" width=\"7\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\"></sup></a></span> </p>\n\n<p>In case you need more details, this is using a convoluted raycasting system I set up.  The projectiles are being fired in the direction of an invisible armorstand summoned 0.1 blocks in front of the player by setting the Motion or Power tags equal to the difference between the coordinates of the armorstand and the player, stored as a scoreboard value, via <span class=\"color-text-highlight-violet\">/data merge</span>.  When I summon them regularly with a <span class=\"color-text-highlight-violet\">/summon</span> command such as <span class=\"color-text-highlight-violet\">/summon minecraft:fireball ~ ~ ~ {direction:[0.0,0.0,0.0],power:[0.123,-0.123,0.246]}</span> they render just fine.  As far as I can tell, it only occurs with <span class=\"color-text-highlight-violet\">/data merge</span>.  I'm not sure if it only affects <span class=\"color-text-highlight-violet\">/data merge</span> with the \"from\" argument, or all <span class=\"color-text-highlight-violet\">/data merge</span> commands.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"Howtoreproduce\"></a>How to reproduce</h3>\n<ol>\n\t<li>Enter the following commands into active repeating command blocks:\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>/summon snowball ~ ~1 ~ {Motion:[1.0,1.0,0.0]}</pre>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>/execute as @e[type=snowball,tag=!edited] run data merge entity @s {Motion:[0.0,1.0,1.0],Tags:[edited]}</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>→ <img class=\"emoticon\" src=\"/images/icons/emoticons/error.png\" height=\"16\" width=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\"> The newest snowballs appear to travel the wrong direction</p></li>\n</ol>\n","customfield_10054":null,"fixVersions":null,"customfield_10055":null,"resolution":null,"customfield_10047":"30/Aug/23 9:09 AM","customfield_10048":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10049":null,"attachment":[{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/23418","id":"23418","filename":"image-2023-08-30-17-02-02-652.png","author":{"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bb0c84ffba7bc327d24083bd0ea08832?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJ-1.png","24x24":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bb0c84ffba7bc327d24083bd0ea08832?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJ-1.png","16x16":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bb0c84ffba7bc327d24083bd0ea08832?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJ-1.png","32x32":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bb0c84ffba7bc327d24083bd0ea08832?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJ-1.png"},"displayName":"j_p_smith","active":true,"timeZone":"Australia/Perth","accountType":"atlassian"},"created":"30/Aug/23 2:02 AM","size":"618 kB","mimeType":"image/png","content":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/23418","thumbnail":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/thumbnail/23418"},{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/23419","id":"23419","filename":"Minecraft 1.21.3 - Singleplayer 2024-10-25 22-05-25.mp4","author":{"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/712020:febf45cf-66f3-400c-a764-a4ff9